<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ethiopia announces interim government in Tigray, aims for polls in six months</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1836ca529d647ae3cedc51fffba8776609edc77911e1b71f45580a9b7858bca4</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T13:05:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261016-ethiopia-announces-interim-government-tigray-calls-for-polls-six-months" /><summary type="html">Ethiopian Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed on Friday announced the appointment of an interim administration to prepare elections in the northern Tigray region previously controlled by the Tigray People's Liberation Front that has clashed with government forces since September. The recent conflict revived a war that killed hundreds of thousands between 2020 and 2022.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>'America, with this president, is not our ally. Trump is a liar': French MEP Bernard Guetta</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da2edcdf1b13d6da92aa312ac0d5910e7c9adb7f2434abe2fb013bc98f7e71df</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T12:55:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261016-america-with-this-president-is-not-our-ally-trump-is-a-liar-french-mep-bernard-guetta" /><summary type="html">Our guest is veteran French journalist and commentator Bernard Guetta, who is a Member of the European Parliament for the centrist Renew group. He tells the programme that Donald Trump is "a liar, because he tried to tell the American people that Zelensky and the Ukrainian resistance were responsible for the price of diesel. This is a pure lie. He (Trump) is responsible because he started the war with Iran." Guetta goes on to say that "without American intelligence sharing, Ukraine is weaker and weaker. That's terrible, to see the president of the United States giving a hand to Putin against Ukraine."</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Thanks a lot, Trump': Wyoming conservatives divided ahead of US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b63a2f7cdbbc970d96dcee09f91f5cb6dc0e4b508759bcb4f8a9180f0df94f01</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T12:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261016-thanks-a-lot-trump-wyoming-conservatives-divided-ahead-us-midterms" /><summary type="html">Famous for its cowboy culture, Wyoming is the least populated, the most rural and the most conservative of all the US states. With two weeks to go until the midterm elections, our reporters James André and Sylvain Rousseau travelled across this Republican stronghold and found that the party of US President Donald Trump is deeply divided in the Cowboy State.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>EU and Canada seek closer ties: Will Canada become the EU's first associate member?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0198d88cfd54ca49c3c68f5a648f56ad9e34730c04d4a1178fdd2d116c9f2c41</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T12:04:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261016-eu-and-canada-seek-closer-ties-will-canada-become-the-eu-s-first-associate-member" /><summary type="html">As the international context becomes more challenging for the European Union, the bloc is looking to boost its ties with like-minded allies. Canada is part of that architecture that the EU says it wants to build. The big news of EU Commission President Ursula von der Leyen's State of the Union speech in September was that Canada could become an associate member – an arrangement that does not exist for the EU's partners at the moment.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>🔴Follow live: 'Ukraine is dependent on Starlink', Zelensky says in Brussels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d328618d7ddd802798ef42f87239b87a551203a421ab77ae4592035c3f73fd14</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T11:46:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-live-trump-calls-renewed-ukraine-attacks-on-russian-oil-refineries-a-disgrace--6cfecd7f8863.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-live-trump-calls-renewed-ukraine-attacks-on-russian-oil-refineries-a-disgrace" /></entry><entry><title>Spring-summer 2027 ready-to-wear collections: Africa in the spotlight at Paris Fashion Week</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e9243e02e1101fb27c2b9a9c38d50437c4b62beeb969b959174ecee047716cf</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T10:58:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/fashion/20261016-spring-summer-2027-ready-to-wear-collections-africa-in-the-spotlight-at-paris-fashion-week" /><summary type="html">Fashion can absolutely be political, when it shapes identities and questions the balance of power. With his label Maxhosa Africa, South Africa's Laduma Ngxokolo is determined to put the continent in the spotlight. In Paris, Jacques Logoh, designer and founder of Togo's International Fashion Festival, gives African creatives a platform on the theme "Fashion against HIV". Plus Mossi Traoré stages his show at Paris's Père Lachaise Cemetery, to tackle the subject of death without taboo.</summary><category term="Fashion" /></entry><entry><title>How books are being scanned and destroyed to train artificial intelligence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07433a8df1d9b1e8fcab13fc4e8bf3aac17fd845494927a9a2c4ee716686a190</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:31:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261016-how-books-are-being-scanned-and-destroyed-to-train-artificial-intelligence" /><summary type="html">To train artificial intelligence models, millions of physical books are being digitised and destroyed. Our colleagues at France 2 investigate this controversial practice and the risk of seeing many rare second-hand books disappear forever.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Shooter kills teacher, three children at Oregon elementary school</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ad5bd8bb29c606451d25ada4b1d315ede564facd81f5c56fe9510cae083b6695</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:27:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261016-shooter-kills-teacher-three-children-at-oregon-elementary-school" /><summary type="html">A teenager shot and killed three children and a teacher on Thursday at an elementary school in the US state of Oregon, police said, adding the assailant was later killed by an armed bystander who pursued him into the building. Officers rushed to Silver Rail Elementary in Bend, a city of about 100,000 in the nation's northwest, after reports of a shooter on campus on Thursday afternoon. The three children who died on the scene were aged five, eight and 11, said Bend police chief Mike Krantz.</summary></entry><entry><title>US considers hitting Iran with 'Mother of All Bombs'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ef241a15bd238813ca510fd0b8d551d9432bba75ac56b24ecef5ed1489a8aef</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:27:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261016-us-considers-hitting-iran-with-mother-of-all-bombs" /><summary type="html">The United States is considering using its biggest non-nuclear bomb against Iran if President Donald Trump should decide to renew combat in the war that has hit a deadlock, CNN reported Thursday. Diplomatic efforts to end the conflict, which erupted with US-Israeli strikes on Iran in February, have been at an impasse since the summer. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Zelensky rallies European allies as Trump ties slump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c376f28b73d12964bb97ebb1dcf9910bfea2593de415a884b8d22ae586b2b7b</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:21:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261016-zelensky-rallies-european-allies-as-trump-ties-slump" /><summary type="html">Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky is seeking to rally European allies at a Brussels summit on Friday after saying Kyiv would no longer abide by US President Donald Trump's demands not to strike Russian oil refineries. Relations between Kyiv and Washington have soured since last week, when Trump eased sanctions on Russia in exchange for Moscow releasing large amounts of diesel onto global markets.</summary></entry><entry><title>EU leaders face budget divisions, discuss Ukraine at Brussels summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f20cf887896759988160247f05f21b5bea818db3aeb3a644c7dfea99495175e</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:20:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261016-eu-leaders-face-budget-divisions-discuss-ukraine-at-brussels-summit" /><summary type="html">European Union leaders gathered in Brussels on Thursday for a two-day summit to discuss the bloc’s next long-term budget, continued support for Ukraine and measures to strengthen Europe’s economic competitiveness amid rising energy prices and geopolitical uncertainty. They voiced strong opposition to a new proposal for the bloc’s long-term budget, raising serious doubt about whether the key spending package will be agreed by the end of year. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating reports from Brussels.</summary></entry><entry><title>France to witness a 'crossroads of anger' as mass protests expected on Saturday</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1169fdc03979440d0d692968a5d28f2713fe5c282a896f25b7f550265babaa76</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T08:53:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261016-france-to-witness-a-crossroads-of-anger-as-mass-protests-expected-on-saturday" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Friday, October 16: French papers look ahead to Saturday's call for mass protests, which will bring together a number of social movements. Next, climate change has devastating consequences on communities in Afghanistan. Also, Libération publishes a special edition written in the style of Georges Perec. Finally, this year's animal of the year has been named.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>No, this oil tanker didn’t carry Russian diesel to the United States</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b025f686b7675e2a50d226565061c49fa530aa61f086812a29ac057dd3d27175</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T08:36:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261016-oil-tanker-carry-russian-diesel-united-states" /><summary type="html">Following US President Donald Trump's October 9 announcement of an agreement signed with Russian President Vladimir Putin to import Russian diesel into the United States, a number of pro-Russian social media accounts began claiming that a Russian oil tanker was already carrying thousands of barrels of diesel to the United States. The ship was actually carrying fertiliser.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Students join Yellow Vest protest: Greater collective strength versus risk of losing distinct voice</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b1a993f6cbfd476a0532c523f958997f8bd6e2cbb477b338e7570bbbf8af492</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T07:41:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-s-student-protests-larger-crowds-risk-overshadowing-students-demands" /><summary type="html">As student protests converge with broader public discontent over the rising cost of living in France, Genie Godula is joined by Sébastien Vieille, national secretary of the SNALC teachers’ union. He offers an assessment of a movement confronting political uncertainty, deteriorating school infrastructure and mounting fiscal constraints. Speaking from Montbéliard in eastern France, Vieille questions whether alliances with larger protest movements, including the Yellow Vests, will strengthen students’ demands or ultimately make them "less visible".</summary></entry><entry><title>Indian authorities detain 'cockroach' movement founder Dipke ahead of new protest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e49f1df95e5dcac5d43c633a844cee1889c2fa8b740179a4e655284de9d0fba5</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T06:39:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261016-indian-authorities-heighten-security-close-park-ahead-cockroach-movement-rally" /><summary type="html">Indian authorities on Friday detained Abhijeet Dipke, the founder of the satirical youth movement "Cockroach Janta Party", ahead of a new protest in New Delhi, live images from the group showed. Police earlier closed a central New Delhi park in an attempt to stifle near-daily demonstrations calling for the election authority chief's resignation over the removal of more than 130 million people from voter lists.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Midterms 2026: Can Democrats capitalise on Latino voter regret?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1ae262867e6113e9c3c9b35d7c94b20f1eb25775effb83e19665fda9926ab3be</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T06:22:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261016-midterms-2026-can-democrats-capitalise-on-latino-voter-regret" /><summary type="html">In 2024, a 46 percent share of the Latino vote helped propel Donald Trump to the White House. But two years on, polls show that support has plummeted in spectacular fashion. Amid an immigration crackdown, violent ICE raids and the spiraling cost of living, some Latino voters say they regret having backed Trump at the ballot box. Now, as the midterms approach, can the Democrats capitalise on this sense of regret to win back what was once an essential part of their base? France 24 reporters Sam Ball and Barbara Gabel met with Latino voters and local Democrats in Phoenix, Arizona, to find out.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK bookstores scramble as Sally Rooney's novels pulled over Palestine Action support</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5bef67d3d7ca66d274d0b47533418fa32444f06d98850fc2dafdd4611d3675dd</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T06:15:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-uk-bookstores-scramble-as-sally-rooney-novels-pulled-over-palestine-action-support" /><summary type="html">Critically acclaimed Irish novelist Sally Rooney's announcement that her books could no longer be sold in the UK due to her support for proscribed group Palestine Action has left British booksellers rushing to stock up on her works before distributors run out. The British government's ban on the group, which practiced non-violent direct action and sabotage against UK military assets believed to be working with the Israeli government, makes support for Palestine Action punishable by up to 14 years in prison.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Marseille's woes continue with second consecutive Europa League defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:faf5f574bdd57f26570f13f2c417aa108ad2851fb957cc37e231545a456f8b86</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T05:41:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261016-marseille-woes-continue-with-a-second-consecutive-europa-league-defeat" /><summary type="html">Things are going from bad to worse for Marseille. The French side suffered their second defeat in as many Europa League matches, losing 1-0 to Olympiakos. Lyon, meanwhile, are heading in the opposite direction, having secured a win over Premier League side Crystal Palace. Rennes, for their part, claimed their first Europa League victory of the season with a narrow 2-1 win over OFI Crete.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Live: Ukraine is ‘dependent’ on Starlink for intercepting Russian drones, Zelensky says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79eb073a6279c673b4238c33dedd9a66ce7e793e49c5ca16703fb16b2b2b9c7a</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T01:50:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-live-trump-calls-renewed-ukraine-attacks-on-russian-oil-refineries-a-disgrace--6cfecd7f8863.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-live-trump-calls-renewed-ukraine-attacks-on-russian-oil-refineries-a-disgrace" /><summary type="html">Ukraine depends on US satellite intelligence service Starlink to intercept jet-powered Russian drones, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said at an EU leaders summit in Brussels Friday. Kyiv was angered this week by disruptions to the critical satellite system hampering its military's ability to counter intense Russian bombardment ahead of the winter months. Follow our liveblog for the latest developments.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Four dead, including three children, in Oregon school shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a02ba6ede6f32c2a3dfffdb493c21313009625c9f70180df3f811f0e11dbf65</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T00:57:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-two-hospitalised-after-shooting-at-oregon-elementary-school-gunman-dead--5a6aa5ab65a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-two-hospitalised-after-shooting-at-oregon-elementary-school-gunman-dead" /></entry><entry><title>Minibus crashes into train at French Channel Tunnel entrance, injuring 19</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74a945b5df9ca47a945da80b8676c8dad115e8586a3d3e65040d6ab36020c571</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T00:53:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-19-injured-as-minibus-crashes-into-train-at-channel-tunnel-entrance--79f37e5f8958.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-19-injured-as-minibus-crashes-into-train-at-channel-tunnel-entrance" /><summary type="html">Nineteen people were injured Thursday when a minibus carrying truck drivers crashed into a vehicle shuttle train at the French entrance to the Channel Tunnel near Calais, forcing a 90-minute suspension of shuttle services. Two people were hospitalised with serious but non-life-threatening injuries, French authorities said.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France and Germany agree to ease EU car emissions rules in new deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a624180c937a26570813e2d62a7d718028c6e1ab7e3bcc1eb74eca9158f1811</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T23:48:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-france-and-germany-agree-to-ease-eu-car-emissions-rules-in-new-deal--9bcf5af8133a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-france-and-germany-agree-to-ease-eu-car-emissions-rules-in-new-deal" /><summary type="html">Paris and Berlin on Friday confirmed their deal aimed at protecting Europe's struggling automotive sector, having reached agreements on the flashpoint issues of EU car emissions and "made in Europe" components. A draft deal reviewed Thursday showed the two countries backing looser EU emissions rules for carmakers.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky rallies European allies as US support for Ukraine wanes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04e0f0f1c1578b1e8297166582405525839e87f80172d1390662fdf23c41101b</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T23:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-zelensky-rallies-european-allies-as-us-support-for-ukraine-wanes--820569914737.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-zelensky-rallies-european-allies-as-us-support-for-ukraine-wanes" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky sought European backing Thursday after vowing to resume strikes on Russian oil refineries despite US President Donald Trump’s demands to stop. Tensions between Kyiv and Washington have escalated in recent days over sanctions, energy infrastructure attacks and restrictions on satellite communications.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Teen shooter kills three children and teacher at Oregon elementary school</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80c5fc35f4465084debb3608785bc058d59ff505e893cf44248f64294dccee2d</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T21:58:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-two-hospitalised-after-shooting-at-oregon-elementary-school-gunman-dead--5a6aa5ab65a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-two-hospitalised-after-shooting-at-oregon-elementary-school-gunman-dead" /><summary type="html">A 16-year-old gunman killed three children and a teacher at Silver Rail Elementary School in Bend, Oregon, on Thursday before being killed by a community member who pursued him inside, police said. Two other people were wounded in the shooting.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
